sn6.2:9.1 starts: all have dwelt,
sn6.2:9.2 starts: will dwell, he dwells,
sn6.2:9.3 starts: revering the true Dhamma.
sn6.2:9.4 starts: This, for Buddhas, is a natural law.
sn7.2:6.1 starts: You live for the good of both
sn7.2:6.2 starts: —your own, the other’s—
sn7.2:6.3 starts: when, knowing the other’s provoked,
sn7.2:6.4 starts: you mindfully grow calm.
sn6.1:2.1 starts: “Enough now with teaching
sn6.1:2.2 starts: what
sn6.1:2.3 starts: This Dhamma is not easily realized
sn6.1:2.4 starts: by those overcome
sn6.1:3.1 starts: What is abstruse, subtle,
sn6.1:3.2 starts: deep,
sn6.1:3.3 starts: those delighting in passion,
sn6.1:3.4 starts: cloaked in the mass of darkness,
sn6.15:11.1 starts: With heart unbowed
sn6.15:11.2 starts: he endured the pain.
sn6.15:11.3 starts: Like a flame’s unbinding
sn6.15:11.4 starts: was the liberation
sn7.2:5.1 starts: You make things worse
sn7.2:5.2 starts: when you flare up
sn7.2:5.3 starts: Whoever doesn’t flare up
sn7.2:5.4 starts: wins a battle
sn7.6:5.1 starts: Where name-&-form,
sn7.6:5.2 starts: along with perception
sn7.6:5.3 starts: totally stop without trace:
sn7.6:5.4 starts: That’s where the tangle
